What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		The /sys/kernel/iommu/ directory contains information about IOMMU
		telemetry. It has two subdirectories:

		- devices: Holds information about each SMMU device.
		- domains: Holds information about each IOMMU domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/enable
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows status of IOMMU telemetry. The value can be either 0 or 1.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/cur_s1_pgtable_usage
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the current S1 pgtable usage in pages.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/max_s1_pgtable_usage
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the maximum S1 pgtable usage in pages, since boot.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/failed_cookie_alloc_count
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the global total number of failed cookie allocations in
		kvm_arm_smmu_alloc_cookie_sg since boot. Excludes cases where nents < 4.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/mode
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the mode of the IOMMU domain. The value can be either
		"pKVM mode" or "non-pKVM mode".

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/type
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the translation type of the IOMMU domain.
		The value can be "S1", "S2", or "Nested".

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/map_sg_count
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the number of iommu_map_sg calls for this domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/map_count
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the total count of page mapping calls executed for this
		domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/unmap_count
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the total count of page unmapping calls executed for this
		domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/avg_sg_list_len
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the average scatterlist length for this domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/smmu
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the smmu to which the domain is attached to.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/attached_devices
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the devices and SIDs associated with this domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/unaligned_64k_mappings
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/unaligned_2m_mappings
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/unaligned_32m_mappings
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/unaligned_512m_mappings
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/unaligned_1g_mappings
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		A non-zero count here means that the IOVA selection has missed
		out on an opportunity to do huge mapping (1 level above block
		mapping). Doing huge mapping improves TLB efficiency and hence
		system performance.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/iova_span
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the total lifetime max IOVA requirement for the domain.
		By default, all domains are working with 3 levels of page tables
		in current version of ARM SMMUv3 driver. However, if some of the
		domains total lifetime max IOVA requirement is well within 1GB
		(in 4K page size case), they can work with 2 levels of page
		tables and that is expected to bring runtime performance
		benefits in doing page table walks. The unit is raw size in bytes.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_4K_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_16K_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_64K_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_2M_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_32M_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_512M_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_1G_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_16G_mapping
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the number of stage-2 mappings for a particular block size.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/num_s2_tlb_invalidates
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the number of stage-2 TLB invalidates.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/prot_mem_usage
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the current memory in bytes that is not mapped for the host (i.e.
		memory carved out from the host stage 2 identity mapping for pKVM and guest
		VM).

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/peak_prot_mem_usage
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the peak memory in bytes that was not mapped for the host since boot.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/s2_atomic_pool_alloc_reqs
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows total S2 page table allocation requests.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/s2_atomic_pool_free_reqs
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows total S2 page table free requests.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/s2_atomic_pool_pages_in_use
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows total S2 page tables in use at the moment

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/stage2-idmap/s2_atomic_pool_max_pages_used
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows maximum S2 page tables in use from the pool since boot

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_4K_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_16K_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_64K_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_2M_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_32M_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_512M_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_1G_mapping
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/domains/<domain_id>/num_16G_mapping
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the number of stage-1 mappings for a particular block size
		for this domain.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/device_id
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the unique ID of the SMMU device.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/cmdq_sync_max_latency_us
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the maximum latency of a command queue sync operation in
		microseconds.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/cmdq_sync_avg_latency_us
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the average latency of a command queue sync operation in
		microseconds.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/cmdq_sync_count
Contact:	Chintan Pandya <chintanpandya@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the number of command queue sync operations.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_bad_streamid_config_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_ste_fetch_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_bad_ste_config_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_stream_disabled_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_bad_substreamid_config_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_cd_fetch_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_bad_cd_config_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_translation_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_addr_size_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_access_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_permission_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_vms_fetch_fault_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/evtq_unknown_fault_count
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the count of SMMU event queue faults of the corresponding type for
		this device.

What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/gerror_sfm_count
What:		/sys/kernel/iommu/devices/<device_name>/gerror_evtq_abt_count
Contact:	Wonbin Jin <wbjin@google.com>
Description:
		Shows the count of SMMU global errors of the corresponding type for
